WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:06.633 --> 00:00:09.866
Hello, my name is Jeff Friedman.

00:00:09.867 --> 00:00:12.099
I'm a professor at the Howard Hughes Medical Institute

00:00:12.100 --> 00:00:13.899
and at Rockefeller University. And I'm pleased to

00:00:13.900 --> 00:00:15.832
be part of the iBiology series.

00:00:15.833 --> 00:00:18.066
Today I'm going to tell you about our research

00:00:18.067 --> 00:00:19.566
into the causes of obesity

00:00:19.567 --> 00:00:22.466
and the discovery of the hormone leptin.

00:00:22.467 --> 00:00:26.699
One of the problems our science addresses

00:00:26.700 --> 00:00:29.832
is obesity. And at some level we'd like to

00:00:29.833 --> 00:00:31.099
understand why it is that some

00:00:31.100 --> 00:00:33.632
individuals have the appearance of

00:00:33.633 --> 00:00:35.999
the child on the left and other people have the

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:37.466
appearance on the right.

00:00:37.467 --> 00:00:40.866
You ask the average person why

00:00:40.867 --> 00:00:42.932
the difference? And most people would say, well

00:00:42.933 --> 00:00:45.366
the individual on the left eats too much.

00:00:45.367 --> 00:00:47.999
Well, that would be true, but it would ignore

00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:50.366
the deeper question of why does the

00:00:50.367 --> 00:00:51.699
individual on the left eat too much?

00:00:51.700 --> 00:00:54.432
And I'd like to try to answer that question

00:00:54.433 --> 00:00:56.032
for you today.

00:00:56.033 --> 00:00:57.532
Now there are several general

00:00:57.533 --> 00:00:59.166
reasons to explain why some individuals

00:00:59.167 --> 00:01:01.099
might eat more than others.

00:01:01.100 --> 00:01:02.966
One possibility is to suggest that

00:01:02.967 --> 00:01:04.699
the obese lack a level of willpower

00:01:04.700 --> 00:01:06.699
that's more evident in lean people.

00:01:06.700 --> 00:01:08.799
I find that point of view is more often

00:01:08.800 --> 00:01:11.466
favored by lean people. Second possibility

00:01:11.467 --> 00:01:13.599
is to suggest that we live in a modern

00:01:13.600 --> 00:01:16.299
environment that predisposes to obesity.

00:01:16.300 --> 00:01:18.432
And a third possibility would be to suggest

00:01:18.433 --> 00:01:20.632
that body weight is controlled by

00:01:20.633 --> 00:01:22.499
biological factors and genes.

00:01:22.500 --> 00:01:24.866
In the interest of time, I'm not going

00:01:24.867 --> 00:01:26.499
to discuss the relative contributions

00:01:26.500 --> 00:01:28.399
of willpower and environment,

00:01:28.400 --> 00:01:30.666
but tell you, in fact, there's substantial

00:01:30.667 --> 00:01:32.466
evidence that genes play a dominant

00:01:32.467 --> 00:01:34.366
role to control body weight.

00:01:34.367 --> 00:01:36.732
There's a number of ways to test

00:01:36.733 --> 00:01:38.799
the genetic contributions to a particular trait.

00:01:38.800 --> 00:01:41.166
The standard way to do so is to systematically

00:01:41.167 --> 00:01:44.132
compare twin pairs.

00:01:44.133 --> 00:01:46.132
Identical twins share all of their genes,

00:01:46.133 --> 00:01:49.132
fraternal twins only share half their genes.

00:01:49.133 --> 00:01:51.632
So if identical twins are more alike

00:01:51.633 --> 00:01:52.999
for a particular trait, then

00:01:53.000 --> 00:01:55.599
non-identical twins we can calculate

00:01:55.600 --> 00:01:58.699
the genetic contribution to that trait.

00:01:58.700 --> 00:02:01.132
If you do this for obesity, what you find

00:02:01.133 --> 00:02:03.299
is that obesity is as or more

00:02:03.300 --> 00:02:05.999
heritable than any trait that's yet been studied,

00:02:06.000 --> 00:02:07.666
with the exception of height.

00:02:07.667 --> 00:02:10.532
In fact, obesity is more heritable than

00:02:10.533 --> 00:02:12.899
many traits that we commonly consider have a genetic

00:02:12.900 --> 00:02:15.299
basis, including schizophrenia, diabetes,

00:02:15.300 --> 00:02:18.032
hypertension, alcoholism, and heart disease.

00:02:18.033 --> 00:02:20.066
In fact, we can calculate based on

00:02:20.067 --> 00:02:23.532
this that about 70-80% of the variation in body

00:02:23.533 --> 00:02:26.299
weight can be ascribed to genetic factors.

00:02:26.300 --> 00:02:28.232
Now to show you the potency of

00:02:28.233 --> 00:02:30.132
these genetic factors to control weight,

00:02:30.133 --> 00:02:32.099
I would like to tell you about a case report.

00:02:32.100 --> 00:02:34.732
This is the child whose image I began by

00:02:34.733 --> 00:02:36.899
showing you, this child was of normal weight

00:02:36.900 --> 00:02:39.099
at birth but began to develop morbid obesity

00:02:39.100 --> 00:02:42.566
very early in life. His parents reported

00:02:42.567 --> 00:02:46.299
intense hyperphagia, intense appetite, to the point where

00:02:46.300 --> 00:02:48.032
they even padlocked the refrigerator

00:02:48.033 --> 00:02:50.432
to keep the child from getting free access

00:02:50.433 --> 00:02:53.166
to food. Despite this, the child kept getting

00:02:53.167 --> 00:02:55.766
fatter and at the age of 4, he weighed

00:02:55.767 --> 00:02:59.032
90lbs and was already pre-diabetic.

00:02:59.033 --> 00:03:01.432
Now this child had a similarly effected

00:03:01.433 --> 00:03:06.699
8 year old cousin who weighed over 200lbs.

00:03:06.700 --> 00:03:09.732
Both these children came from an inbred family

00:03:09.733 --> 00:03:11.999
and often times when you seen an extreme

00:03:12.000 --> 00:03:14.366
phenotype in an inbred family, in this case,

00:03:14.367 --> 00:03:16.099
as a result of a first cousin marriage,

00:03:16.100 --> 00:03:19.032
it's a result of a genetic alteration.

00:03:19.033 --> 00:03:21.399
So Steve O'Rahilly and colleagues

00:03:21.400 --> 00:03:24.099
suggested that perhaps this child was

00:03:24.100 --> 00:03:25.866
obese as the result of a mutation

00:03:25.867 --> 00:03:28.532
in a particular gene. And they hypothesized

00:03:28.533 --> 00:03:31.166
that this child might be missing a hormone

00:03:31.167 --> 00:03:33.999
leptin that was first identified by my laboratory.

00:03:34.000 --> 00:03:36.832
Leptin is a hormone made by fat tissue

00:03:36.833 --> 00:03:39.332
that's secreted into the blood where it circulates,

00:03:39.333 --> 00:03:42.966
ultimately acting on the brain to regulate

00:03:42.967 --> 00:03:46.899
food intake. In the absence of leptin,

00:03:46.900 --> 00:03:50.166
animals eat more and so, O'Rahilly suggested

00:03:50.167 --> 00:03:52.866
that perhaps this child was missing the hormone leptin.

00:03:52.867 --> 00:03:54.699
They tested and indeed, the child was

00:03:54.700 --> 00:03:58.132
missing leptin. So they decided to now take leptin

00:03:58.133 --> 00:04:00.499
that was made in the laboratory and give it back

00:04:00.500 --> 00:04:02.532
to this child. And what you can see is

00:04:02.533 --> 00:04:04.432
that the child from between the ages of 4

00:04:04.433 --> 00:04:07.332
and 6, lost a substantial amount of weight, despite

00:04:07.333 --> 00:04:10.032
getting taller. In addition, the child

00:04:10.033 --> 00:04:12.532
ate less. Before the first leptin injection

00:04:12.533 --> 00:04:14.666
he ate 2000 calories in a single meal,

00:04:14.667 --> 00:04:17.132
after a few leptin injections, the child now

00:04:17.133 --> 00:04:20.032
ate a 180 calories at the same meal,

00:04:20.033 --> 00:04:22.532
which is the appropriate number of calories for a child

00:04:22.533 --> 00:04:23.932
of that age and size.

00:04:23.933 --> 00:04:27.066
In this case the child was obese

00:04:27.067 --> 00:04:29.199
because of a defect in the hormone leptin,

00:04:29.200 --> 00:04:31.432
without leptin no signal is ever generated

00:04:31.433 --> 00:04:33.066
that there are adequate fat stores.

00:04:33.067 --> 00:04:36.032
This is a stimulus to eat more and this child

00:04:36.033 --> 00:04:39.499
kept eating, kept getting fatter, without ever making

00:04:39.500 --> 00:04:41.632
the signal to shut the system off.

00:04:41.633 --> 00:04:43.299
And now here's a picture of the child

00:04:43.300 --> 00:04:45.566
at the age of 8, it's the same child I began

00:04:45.567 --> 00:04:48.199
by showing you a picture of. So this child

00:04:48.200 --> 00:04:50.799
was obese, not as a lack of will power

00:04:50.800 --> 00:04:53.166
or a toxic environment; this child was obese

00:04:53.167 --> 00:04:56.066
because a lack of a hormone leptin.

00:04:56.067 --> 00:04:59.132
Studies of this child and other individuals

00:04:59.133 --> 00:05:01.232
has now suggested that body weight is regulated

00:05:01.233 --> 00:05:03.366
by a hormonal loop, of which leptin

00:05:03.367 --> 00:05:05.099
is an important component.

00:05:05.100 --> 00:05:08.166
At our stable weight, food intake

00:05:08.167 --> 00:05:10.832
equals energy expenditure and we make a particular

00:05:10.833 --> 00:05:13.666
amount of leptin. Now imagine if that

00:05:13.667 --> 00:05:18.432
mass falls after a diet, leptin level would fall.

00:05:18.433 --> 00:05:21.432
A low leptin level will be provide a stimulus

00:05:21.433 --> 00:05:24.066
to eat more, much as the same as the case

00:05:24.067 --> 00:05:26.099
of the untreated leptin-deficient child,

00:05:26.100 --> 00:05:28.766
and now, an individual will have a potent

00:05:28.767 --> 00:05:31.332
stimulus to their appetite until such time

00:05:31.333 --> 00:05:33.199
as their fat mass and leptin level returns

00:05:33.200 --> 00:05:34.632
to the starting point.

00:05:34.633 --> 00:05:37.066
Conversely, if you overeat for a period

00:05:37.067 --> 00:05:40.999
of time, binge-eating, fat mass goes up and leptin

00:05:41.000 --> 00:05:43.232
levels go up with it. This will suppress

00:05:43.233 --> 00:05:45.932
appetite, again, until such time the fat mass

00:05:45.933 --> 00:05:48.032
and leptin level return to the starting point.

00:05:48.033 --> 00:05:50.866
So because leptin is made in proportion

00:05:50.867 --> 00:05:52.832
to fat mass, it provides a signal

00:05:52.833 --> 00:05:55.832
that can then control food intake and

00:05:55.833 --> 00:05:58.566
the response to weight loss or weight gain.

00:05:58.567 --> 00:06:00.432
And what this system does in a sense

00:06:00.433 --> 00:06:02.599
is set up a biological response that

00:06:02.600 --> 00:06:04.299
resists weight change in either direction.

00:06:04.300 --> 00:06:07.066
If you lose fat mass, leptin level falls

00:06:07.067 --> 00:06:08.666
and there's stimulus to gain weight.

00:06:08.667 --> 00:06:11.232
If you gain fat mass, leptin level rises

00:06:11.233 --> 00:06:14.566
and that suppresses appetite. And by this

00:06:14.567 --> 00:06:16.932
mechanism, body weight can be maintained within

00:06:16.933 --> 00:06:18.799
a relatively narrow range.

00:06:18.800 --> 00:06:21.666
Now, if you hear all of this and find that there

00:06:21.667 --> 00:06:25.132
was an undiscovered hormone circulating in the blood of animals

00:06:25.133 --> 00:06:28.532
and humans, it seems rather mysterious

00:06:28.533 --> 00:06:31.066
to consider how this hormone was identified.

00:06:31.067 --> 00:06:32.932
So I'd like to now tell you about how

00:06:32.933 --> 00:06:35.032
I became interested in this hormone and how

00:06:35.033 --> 00:06:36.399
it was discovered.

00:06:36.400 --> 00:06:38.899
My interest in this area began with

00:06:38.900 --> 00:06:42.366
an interest in behavior. How molecules control behavior

00:06:42.367 --> 00:06:45.999
and my first interest centered on another

00:06:46.000 --> 00:06:47.666
hormone that's said to regulate appetite,

00:06:47.667 --> 00:06:51.832
CCK. Cholecystokinin is made by

00:06:51.833 --> 00:06:54.032
endocrine cells in your intestine in response to

00:06:54.033 --> 00:06:56.166
food. When food is present

00:06:56.167 --> 00:06:58.266
inside your gut, CCK is secreted

00:06:58.267 --> 00:07:00.632
into the blood and it stimulates

00:07:00.633 --> 00:07:02.932
the contraction of your gallbladder and

00:07:02.933 --> 00:07:05.332
secretion of enzymes by your pancreas

00:07:05.333 --> 00:07:06.832
that aid in digestion.

00:07:06.833 --> 00:07:09.732
And this was the situation in 1968,

00:07:09.733 --> 00:07:12.532
prior to the work of Smith and Gibbs, who also

00:07:12.533 --> 00:07:15.332
showed that CCK can suppress appetite.

00:07:15.333 --> 00:07:19.999
They suggested in fact, that this intestinal hormone

00:07:20.000 --> 00:07:22.699
when it's secreted, not only helps aid digestion

00:07:22.700 --> 00:07:25.266
but also circulates in the blood and acts on

00:07:25.267 --> 00:07:27.832
the brain to shut off a meal.

00:07:27.833 --> 00:07:31.066
Made perfect sense, excitement in this area

00:07:31.067 --> 00:07:33.666
was amplified when a few years later,

00:07:33.667 --> 00:07:36.299
CCK was also found in the brain

00:07:36.300 --> 00:07:38.432
by a group led by Graham Dockray.

00:07:38.433 --> 00:07:40.599
This then suggested that perhaps

00:07:40.600 --> 00:07:43.166
appetite and body weight are regulated

00:07:43.167 --> 00:07:46.166
by a hormone that is expressed in both

00:07:46.167 --> 00:07:48.299
the gut and the brain. And that the levels

00:07:48.300 --> 00:07:52.132
peripherally synthesized in brain synthesized

00:07:52.133 --> 00:07:55.066
CCK might control food intake and

00:07:55.067 --> 00:07:57.999
body weight. And this was referred to at the time

00:07:58.000 --> 00:07:59.299
as the "gut-brain" axis.

00:07:59.300 --> 00:08:02.266
Interest in this area was amplified even further

00:08:02.267 --> 00:08:05.266
in 1970 when Straus and Yalow reported

00:08:05.267 --> 00:08:08.066
that the levels of CCK were reduced in the brains

00:08:08.067 --> 00:08:12.632
of a strange genetically obese mouse, known as the ob mouse.

00:08:12.633 --> 00:08:16.332
The ob mouse as a result of a defect in a single

00:08:16.333 --> 00:08:19.432
gene, and Yalow and Straus suggested that that

00:08:19.433 --> 00:08:21.799
affected gene might be CCK, this endogenous

00:08:21.800 --> 00:08:24.632
appetite suppresant. With a lower level

00:08:24.633 --> 00:08:26.199
of the endogenous appetite suppressant,

00:08:26.200 --> 00:08:28.799
the animals might eat more.

00:08:28.800 --> 00:08:30.799
Well, this is a picture of the ob mouse.

00:08:30.800 --> 00:08:34.099
The animal on the far right is an ob mouse,

00:08:34.100 --> 00:08:38.866
and the animal second from the right

00:08:38.867 --> 00:08:40.699
is a lean littermate of that animal.

00:08:40.700 --> 00:08:42.732
The only defect between the ob mouse

00:08:42.733 --> 00:08:44.932
and its sibling littermate is a defect

00:08:44.933 --> 00:08:47.866
in a single gene. That single genetic defect

00:08:47.867 --> 00:08:50.666
leads the ob animal to eat more, more around

00:08:50.667 --> 00:08:52.899
less, ultimately weigh three times as much

00:08:52.900 --> 00:08:54.932
and having five times as much fat

00:08:54.933 --> 00:08:56.366
as the sibling littermate.

00:08:56.367 --> 00:08:59.066
And as I mentioned, Yalow suggested that

00:08:59.067 --> 00:09:01.132
perhaps this animal overate

00:09:01.133 --> 00:09:03.099
because it was missing CCK,

00:09:03.100 --> 00:09:05.066
this endogenous appetite suppressant.

00:09:05.067 --> 00:09:07.066
The only problem with this idea

00:09:07.067 --> 00:09:09.399
is that it very might well be wrong.

00:09:09.400 --> 00:09:11.432
And this had to do with the fact that

00:09:11.433 --> 00:09:13.399
the person I was working with at the time,

00:09:13.400 --> 00:09:16.432
Bruce Schneider, published a contemporaneous report

00:09:16.433 --> 00:09:18.432
showing that the levels of CCK

00:09:18.433 --> 00:09:21.899
in brain were no different in ob mice versus

00:09:21.900 --> 00:09:23.099
their lean littermates.

00:09:23.100 --> 00:09:25.666
And so, we and others wondered whether or not

00:09:25.667 --> 00:09:27.366
CCK was the defective gene

00:09:27.367 --> 00:09:28.932
in the ob animals.

00:09:28.933 --> 00:09:31.099
Well, one of the first things we did

00:09:31.100 --> 00:09:33.466
at the time was to clone the CCK

00:09:33.467 --> 00:09:35.366
gene. And the idea was to clone

00:09:35.367 --> 00:09:37.799
the CCK gene and see where on the

00:09:37.800 --> 00:09:39.866
chromosome it mapped, whether it mapped

00:09:39.867 --> 00:09:42.399
near the location of the ob gene.

00:09:42.400 --> 00:09:44.766
We quickly found that CCK mapped to the

00:09:44.767 --> 00:09:46.266
distal end of Chromosome 9.

00:09:46.267 --> 00:09:48.999
This is a map of Chromosome 9 with a variety

00:09:49.000 --> 00:09:50.866
of genes that map there. The only

00:09:50.867 --> 00:09:53.599
problem was that the ob gene didn't map

00:09:53.600 --> 00:09:56.666
to Chromosome 9, it mapped to Chromosome 6.

00:09:56.667 --> 00:09:59.799
So these data excluded the possibility

00:09:59.800 --> 00:10:01.199
that CCK was the ob gene.

00:10:01.200 --> 00:10:03.932
And raised the question, well if it's not

00:10:03.933 --> 00:10:05.432
CCK, what is it?

00:10:05.433 --> 00:10:08.266
In the 1980s when we did this work,

00:10:08.267 --> 00:10:10.666
a new technology was emerging that allowed

00:10:10.667 --> 00:10:12.332
one to identify defective genes,

00:10:12.333 --> 00:10:14.399
not based on knowledge of their function,

00:10:14.400 --> 00:10:17.632
but simply based on detailed knowledge

00:10:17.633 --> 00:10:19.899
of the chromosomal location of that gene.

00:10:19.900 --> 00:10:22.566
This methodology was known as positional

00:10:22.567 --> 00:10:24.999
cloning, and we set out then to identify

00:10:25.000 --> 00:10:27.699
the ob gene using positional cloning.

00:10:27.700 --> 00:10:33.166
This required identifying genes in the region

00:10:33.167 --> 00:10:35.632
of the chromosome where ob was known to map.

00:10:35.633 --> 00:10:37.999
And one day, on a Friday, we found

00:10:38.000 --> 00:10:40.199
a gene in the region of ob that was expressed only

00:10:40.200 --> 00:10:43.866
in fat tissue. This is a Northern blot, it's a way at the time

00:10:43.867 --> 00:10:46.632
of measuring RNA levels and only

00:10:46.633 --> 00:10:48.632
fat tissue had an RNA for this gene,

00:10:48.633 --> 00:10:50.632
which we knew mapped near the ob gene.

00:10:50.633 --> 00:10:52.566
The next step was to ask, is

00:10:52.567 --> 00:10:55.266
this gene defective in strains of mice

00:10:55.267 --> 00:10:56.932
that are genetically obese?

00:10:56.933 --> 00:10:58.599
And indeed it was.

00:10:58.600 --> 00:11:00.799
If you look here at lane 2, that's fat tissue

00:11:00.800 --> 00:11:03.166
from a normal mouse. Lane 3 is fat

00:11:03.167 --> 00:11:04.966
tissue from an ob mouse of the same

00:11:04.967 --> 00:11:08.799
strain. That strain fails to make the ob

00:11:08.800 --> 00:11:10.766
RNA and that's why it's fat.

00:11:10.767 --> 00:11:13.666
Lane 4 is RNA is fat tissue of a different strain

00:11:13.667 --> 00:11:16.932
of mouse and lane 5 is RNA from

00:11:16.933 --> 00:11:20.266
the obese animal from that same strain.

00:11:20.267 --> 00:11:22.899
In this case, increased levels of RNA are produced

00:11:22.900 --> 00:11:25.066
and that's because the RNA produces

00:11:25.067 --> 00:11:28.232
a defective protein. The animal then makes more and more

00:11:28.233 --> 00:11:30.632
RNA as a means of trying to compensate,

00:11:30.633 --> 00:11:33.132
unsuccessfully, because the RNA makes a defective

00:11:33.133 --> 00:11:36.599
protein. Well, the demonstration that

00:11:36.600 --> 00:11:38.166
this gene was defective in two

00:11:38.167 --> 00:11:39.799
different obese strains of mice

00:11:39.800 --> 00:11:42.199
confirmed that we had in fact identified

00:11:42.200 --> 00:11:44.299
the defective gene, and this was published

00:11:44.300 --> 00:11:48.132
to some fanfare in 1994 with this image

00:11:48.133 --> 00:11:50.266
of an obese mouse outweighing two

00:11:50.267 --> 00:11:52.066
of its sibling littermates.

00:11:52.067 --> 00:11:54.732
Shortly after identifying the ob gene,

00:11:54.733 --> 00:11:56.932
subsequent studies revealed, in fact,

00:11:56.933 --> 00:11:58.866
that the defective gene encoded this hormone

00:11:58.867 --> 00:12:00.866
leptin. It's the hormone made by fat

00:12:00.867 --> 00:12:03.266
tissue that regulates appetite by

00:12:03.267 --> 00:12:06.232
acting on brain centers.

00:12:06.233 --> 00:12:08.999
One of the key experiments was done by

00:12:09.000 --> 00:12:11.699
collaborators Jeff Halaas and Ketan Gajiwala and Steve

00:12:11.700 --> 00:12:14.299
Burley, together we showed that if you inject

00:12:14.300 --> 00:12:16.632
saline into an ob animal nothing happens,

00:12:16.633 --> 00:12:19.332
they stay obese. But if you inject leptin

00:12:19.333 --> 00:12:21.266
made in the laboratory, animals normalize

00:12:21.267 --> 00:12:23.732
their phenotype. Much the same as O'Rahilly

00:12:23.733 --> 00:12:26.299
and colleagues later showed for this leptin

00:12:26.300 --> 00:12:27.666
deficient child.

00:12:27.667 --> 00:12:30.099
Now leptin mutations are quite rare,

00:12:30.100 --> 00:12:31.966
there are only a few dozen such mutations

00:12:31.967 --> 00:12:34.232
in the world, which is characteristic of hormones

00:12:34.233 --> 00:12:36.199
which are poor targets for mutations.

00:12:36.200 --> 00:12:39.766
But we now know that perhaps 10-15%

00:12:39.767 --> 00:12:41.532
of morbid obesity is the result of

00:12:41.533 --> 00:12:44.166
single gene defects in other genes

00:12:44.167 --> 00:12:47.166
in the neural circuit on which leptin acts.

00:12:47.167 --> 00:12:49.299
And so this has provided a great stimulus

00:12:49.300 --> 00:12:52.932
in research into the causes of obesity,

00:12:52.933 --> 00:12:55.999
and tells us now that obesity is very often

00:12:56.000 --> 00:12:57.932
a result of specific genetic defects.

00:12:57.933 --> 00:13:00.532
I suspect that we'll identify ever more

00:13:00.533 --> 00:13:02.632
of these defects now, with advances in DNA

00:13:02.633 --> 00:13:05.299
sequencing and other new technologies.

00:13:05.300 --> 00:13:07.166
And so I think research in this

00:13:07.167 --> 00:13:08.899
area has been greatly stimulated by the

00:13:08.900 --> 00:13:11.699
identification of leptin and the realization

00:13:11.700 --> 00:13:14.366
that obesity can be the result of genetic defects

00:13:14.367 --> 00:13:17.532
in a neural circuit that regulates food intake

00:13:17.533 --> 00:13:18.533
and body weight.

